<title>USA: Media General completes acquisition.</title>
<headline>Media General completes acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Media General Inc said on Friday it completed its $48 million purchase of the Potomac News from Community Newspaper Holdings Inc, and its sale of 43 daily and weekly newspapers to Community Newspaper for $107 million.</p>
<p>The Potomac News, in Woodbridge, Va., has a daily and Sunday circulation of 31,000.  It was acquired by Community Newspaper from Garden State Newspapers Inc, then sold to Media General in an exchange for the 43 properties Media General recently acquired from Park Acquisitions Inc.</p>
<p>The 43 newspapers acquired by Community Newspaper are in Georgia, Idaho, Indiana, Illinois, New York, North Carolina, North Dakota and Oklahoma.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
